  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multidisciplinary Forensic Assistance for the Mexican State Institutions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mexico is confronting a humanitarian crisis with over 111,000 people reported as Disappeared or missing, and 1660 in Nayarit according to the National Registry of Disappeared and Unidentified Persons. The situation has overwhelmed the forensic capacity of corresponding state institutions and led to a backlog of more than 52,000 unidentified bodies. In this context, in this three-year-project, Forensic Anthropology Foundation of Guatemala (FAFG) will strengthen local Mexican State forensic capacity in Nayarit in coordination with State Search Commissions (CEB), Forensic Services, and the Special Prosecutor&apos;s Office. Specific Objectives are 1)training to forensic personnel 2)Develop procedures and tools for the investigation of disappeared persons 3)facilitate strategic coordination among local institutions and 4) ensure implementation of a Multidisciplinary Human Identification System in Nayarit.</narrative>
  </description>
